<title>NETHERLANDS: DUTCH SHELL CUTS GASOLINE, DIESEL PRICES.</title>
<headline>DUTCH SHELL CUTS GASOLINE, DIESEL PRICES.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Royal Dutch/Shell unit Shell Nederland BV said on Monday it would cut its retail prices for gasoline in the Netherlands by one cent per litre with effect from Wednesday May 14.</p>
<p>The move reflects changes in international product prices and the value of the dollar against the guilder, the company said.</p>
<p>From Wednesday the price of premium unleaded gasoline at Shell's self-service stations will fall to 2.09 guilders per litre.</p>
<p>The price of premium with lead substitute falls to 2.16 guilders and Euro regular unleaded to 2.04 guilders.</p>
<p>The recommended price for diesel goes down to 1.448 guilders per litre, Shell said.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000</p>
</text>
